      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That \"thud\" of pain is a classic sign of a severe migraine, and I'm not going to tell you to take an extra dose of sumatriptan because it could lead to a dangerous serotonin syndrome. Instead, you should immediately take a full dose of your prescribed sumatriptan combined with a non-prescription NSAID like ibuprofen or naproxen to break the pain cycle. If you feel nauseous, take a ginger supplement or ginger ale to settle your stomach, but do not wait until you feel worse to seek help. Your body is built to handle this, and I'm here to guide you through it safely.",
